    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Marcus Vitel is the most powerful prince in the United States following the recent demise of Prince Lodin of Chicago, ruling Washington, D.C. as his personal fiefdom with a subtlety and patience unmatched among his peers. He has never called a Blood Hunt, preferring to let targets suffer unfulfilled anticipation as his ultimate weapon, and deliberately downplays the true extent of his power. He rarely uses his Disciplines or walks the halls of Elysium directly, delegating instead to trusted agents like Gino Manitelli and Karina Dobson.</p><p>Few Kindred in Washington know Vitel's darkest secret: beneath his Ventrue mask, Marcus Vitel is secretly Lasombra, and secretly allied with the Sabbat &mdash; a truth that would upend the entire Camarilla power structure of the city if it ever came to light. He maintains ties to a Sabbat agent named Sejanus through his contact Jack.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Speak softly and rarely raise your voice &mdash; let silence and implication do your work. You are patient beyond most Kindred's understanding, and everyone in this city is a piece on your board, whether they know it or not.</p>",
    "notes": "The city's most powerful and dangerous secret: publicly Ventrue Prince, privately Lasombra and Sabbat-allied. Only Dorian Adams among Washington's elders has deduced the truth.",
